<title>FRANCE: French March trade surplus 9.82 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French March trade surplus 9.82 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>France had a seasonally adjusted trade surplus in March of 9.82 billion francs compared with a revised surplus in February  of 11.35 billion, provisional customs office data reported on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The office had originally reported a surplus in February of 11.37 billion francs.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures, in billions of francs and seasonally adjusted unless otherwise stated, were as follows:</p>
<p>					  March    Feb</p>
<p> Trade balance			9.817  11.351</p>
<p> Trade balance (unadjusted)    16.619  11.186</p>
<p> Imports			    120.635 118.318</p>
<p> Exports			    130.452 129.669</p>
<p> Agri-business balance	    5.213   5.369</p>
<p> Energy balance		    -8.588  -8.367</p>
<p> Industrial/military balance    8.874  10.163</p>
<p> Airbus exports	 4.235 (9 planes)  3.726 (7)</p>
<p> Defence (unadj)		   1.993    0.866</p>
<p> Unadjusted exports	     139.210 126.348</p>
<p> Unadjusted imports	     122.591 115.162</p>
<p> European Union		     4.751   7.114</p>
<p> Germany				0.420   0.294</p>
<p> Japan				 -1.439  -1.223</p>
<p> United States		     -3.240  -1.982</p>
<p>Cumulative figures for the first three months of the year were as follows</p>
<p>				     Jan-Mar 1997     Jan-Mar 1996</p>
<p> Before seasonal adjustment    33.696	     19.460</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted	     32.424	     19.404</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 54 52</p>
